---
// Life hacks: a sub-tab of the Management tab (#life-hacks). Deo's own words, numbered in his order.
// Life hack #2 holds the calendar text that used to sit on the PM side; the PM side links here.
---

<p class="ranking-lede hacks-lede">The small systems that keep my days, and my brain, running.</p>

<ol class="hacks">
  <li id="hack-pm-your-life">
    <span class="hack-rank" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
    <div class="hack-body">
      <h3><span class="sr-only">Life hack #1: </span>PM your life!</h3>
      <p>
        Treat your life like a project: break big goals into small steps, be honest about scope and deadlines, and track what's
        actually done. It's how I run everything from client work to this website, and the <a href="#pm">PM side</a> of this tab
        has the details.
      </p>
    </div>
  </li>
  <li id="hack-calendar-bound">
    <span class="hack-rank" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
    <div class="hack-body">
      <h3><span class="sr-only">Life hack #2: </span>Calendar bound</h3>
      <p>
        If it's tied to a date, it goes on the calendar. OneCalendar merges my 5+
        calendars into one master calendar, shown as a widget front and center on my phone. As soon as I wake up, I have a rough
        idea of how the day will go, and I plan around the hard commitments.
      </p>
    </div>
  </li>
  <li id="hack-shisa-kanko">
    <span class="hack-rank" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
    <div class="hack-body">
      <h3>
        <span class="sr-only">Life hack #3: </span>Shisa Kanko <span lang="ja" translate="no">(指差喚呼)</span>
      </h3>
      <p>
        Shisa Kanko, "pointing and calling", comes from Japan's railways: you point at the thing you're checking and say it out
        loud. Human brains are made to conserve energy, and everything that can become automatic eventually becomes automatic.
      </p>
      <p>
        This is especially useful for ADHD-leaning brains, as a way to force monotropic focus on whatever needs a crosscheck. When
        I want to confirm the garage is closed, I raise my hand toward it and say "garage closed". That works like a system-wide
        interrupt to my many ongoing thought channels, so my brain actually stores that the garage is closed before I drive away.
      </p>
    </div>
  </li>
  <li id="hack-systematize-your-brain">
    <span class="hack-rank" aria-hidden="true">4</span>
    <div class="hack-body">
      <h3><span class="sr-only">Life hack #4: </span>Systematize your brain</h3>
      <p>
        This one is especially powerful for AuDHD brains. It's a way to force the creation of an inner council, where the opposing
        forces meet in the middle and help steer the boat together instead of fighting each other.
      </p>
      <p>
        As a software developer, I began treating parts of my brain like an OS (as you can clearly see from how I decompose my
        brain across this website). It puts structure and bounds around the immense energy that lives within me. That energy is a
        well, and it can run dry if it isn't cared for. All this scaffolding is there to protect me from myself, and to protect me
        from people who would abuse and steal from that same well without giving anything back.
      </p>
    </div>
  </li>
</ol>

<style>
  .hacks-lede {
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }
  .hacks {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    max-width: 72ch;
  }
  .hacks li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 3rem 1fr;
    gap: 1rem;
    align-items: start;
    padding: 1.1rem 1.25rem;
    border-radius: 16px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(190, 200, 209, 0.15);
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);
  }
  .hack-rank {
    font-size: 2rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--teal, #39c5bb);
    text-align: center;
  }
  .hacks h3 {
    margin: 0.1rem 0 0.5rem;
    font-size: var(--step-1, 1.25rem);
  }
  .hacks p {
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
  }
  .hacks p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
  @media (max-width: 520px) {
    .hacks li {
      grid-template-columns: 2rem 1fr;
      gap: 0.75rem;
      padding: 1rem;
    }
    .hack-rank {
      font-size: 1.6rem;
    }
  }
</style>
